    <statement><p>Calculate the derivative using the appropriate rule or combination of rules.
<me>g(z)=\frac{z^{2}+8z+16}{z+1}\frac{z^{2}-3z-4}{z+4}</me></p>
<p><m>g'(z) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2z</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>g(z)=\frac{z^{2}+8z+16}{z+1}\frac{z^{2}-3z-4}{z+4}=\frac{\left(z+4\right)\mathopen{}\left(z+4\right)}{z+1}\frac{\left(z-4\right)\mathopen{}\left(z+1\right)}{z+4}.</me>
<m>g(z)=\left(z+4\right)\mathopen{}\left(z-4\right)</m>, assuming <m>z \ne -4</m> and <m>z \ne -1</m>, whence
<me>g'(z)=(z-4)(1)+(z+4)(1)=2z.</me>


</solution>
